---
/** Present frozen study indices, observed browser coverage, and exact isolated prototypes. */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import AgenticNav from "../../components/AgenticNav.astro";
import ResourceAbout from "../../components/ResourceAbout.astro";
import { AXES, CHECKS, STUDY_TITLE, label, number, recordLabel, studyView } from "../../lib/flower-study-model.mjs";
import results from "../../../public/agentic-le/flower-study/results.json";
import index from "../../../public/agentic-le/flower-study/publication-index.json";
const view = studyView(results, index);
const base = "/agentic-le/flower-study/";
const published = new Date(index.prepared_at_utc).toLocaleString("en-GB", {timeZone: "UTC", day: "numeric", month: "long", year: "numeric", hour: "2-digit", minute: "2-digit", hour12: false}) + " UTC";
const qa = index.browser_summary.functional;
const state = value => ({completed: "Complete", failed: "Failed", cancelled: "Cancelled", skipped: "Skipped"}[value] ?? value);
const checkState = (candidate, key) => candidate.browser?.checks?.find(check => check.check_id === key)?.status ?? "Not observed";
---
<Base title={`${STUDY_TITLE} · Capability Matters`} description="The completed five-condition flower study: separate evidence-based rubric indices, reviewer disagreement, browser-check coverage, and retained prototypes.">
  <AgenticNav active="study" />
  <div class="study-shell">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Learning engineering flower · Actual study records</p>
      <h1>{STUDY_TITLE}</h1>
      <ResourceAbout resource="agentic-flower-study" />
      <div class="study-banner"><strong>Generation records and model reviews frozen</strong><p>Publication data prepared <time datetime={index.prepared_at_utc}>{published}</time>. This view replaces the meeting snapshot with the complete planned candidate set, including missing evidence.</p></div>
      <p>Five configurations addressed the same fictional challenge: helping new team leads practise a difficult feedback conversation. Three repetitions were planned per configuration. The results describe generated learning solutions and repeated model judgments; no human outcomes were measured.</p>
      <nav class="page-actions" aria-label="Study sections"><a class="primary" href="#results">Compare the three axes</a><a href="#prototypes">Inspect the prototypes</a><a href="/agentic-le/paper/">Read the paper</a><button id="copy-link">Copy study link</button><span id="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></nav>
      <div class="metrics"><div><strong>{view.buildCount}/{index.planned_candidates}</strong><span>evaluated Build previews</span></div><div><strong>{results.accepted_review_count}/{results.review_count}</strong><span>accepted model-review attempts</span></div><div><strong>{qa.bound_candidates}/{index.planned_candidates}</strong><span>candidates with verified browser records</span></div><div><strong>3 axes</strong><span>reported separately</span></div></div>
    </header>

    <section id="results" aria-labelledby="results-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Descriptive comparison · Fixed condition order</p><h2 id="results-title">Three views of the same evidence</h2>
      <p>These <strong>0–100 rubric indices</strong> summarize 0–4 criterion ratings. They are not percentages of learners, probabilities, or measured human outcomes. Each candidate index requires both reviewers to rate all three criteria on that axis. Unknown values remain unknown.</p>
      {view.excluded.size > 0 && <p class="missing-note"><strong>{view.reviews.size} of {index.planned_candidates} planned candidates are included in the review set.</strong> The batch reports completion for all generation runs, but {view.excluded.size} candidate has no verified terminal record and is excluded from evaluation. Its card below retains the reason; it receives no rating or evaluated preview.</p>}
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Condition-level rubric indices"><table><caption>Condition means and sample standard deviations across generated candidates</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Condition</th>{AXES.map(([,name]) => <th scope="col">{name}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{view.conditions.map(condition => <tr><th scope="row"><a href={`#condition-${condition.key}`}>{condition.name}</a><span class="cell-note">{condition.candidates.length} planned candidates</span></th>{AXES.map(([axis]) => {
        const value = condition.group?.axes[axis];
        const known = value?.observed_count ?? 0;
        const unknown = value?.unknown_count ?? 0;
        const excluded = condition.candidates.length - (condition.group?.candidate_count ?? 0);
        return <td><strong class="index-value">{number(value?.mean)}</strong><span class="cell-note">SD {value?.sd == null ? "not estimable" : number(value.sd)} · {known}/{condition.candidates.length} known</span>{(unknown > 0 || excluded > 0) && <span class="cell-note">{unknown} unknown rating · {excluded} excluded from review</span>}</td>;
      })}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p class="small">The table uses candidate means from the frozen aggregate without imputation. Standard deviation describes the spread of known candidate indices; it is unavailable with fewer than two known values. Repeated reviews and criteria are not additional generated candidates. There is no combined score or overall rank.</p>
      {index.figure && <figure><img src={`${base}${index.figure.file}`} alt={index.figure.alt} loading="lazy" /><figcaption>{index.figure.caption}</figcaption></figure>}
      <details class="method-detail"><summary>How the indices and reviewer pairs work</summary><p>Each review rates nine criteria, three on each axis. An axis index is twenty-five times the mean of its three 0–4 ratings. The displayed candidate value is the mean of two complete reviewer indices. A missing criterion makes that reviewer’s axis unknown; a missing reviewer index makes the candidate axis unknown.</p><p>Two fresh calls to the same model ({results.model}, reasoning effort {results.reasoning_effort}) produced the reviewer pair. These are repeated model judgments, not independent human raters. Failed review attempts remain in the record as unknown values. Exact evidence quotations support traceability, not the correctness of a judgment.</p><p><a href={`${base}results.json`}>Frozen aggregate JSON</a> · <a href={`${base}raw-ratings.csv`}>Raw criterion ratings (CSV)</a></p></details>
    </section>

    <section id="conditions" aria-labelledby="conditions-title"><h2 id="conditions-title">What each contrast changes</h2><div class="condition-list">{view.conditions.map(condition => <article id={`condition-${condition.key}`}><h3>{condition.name}</h3><p>{condition.description}</p></article>)}</div><p>Assessment, Measurement, Evaluation is the domain manipulated here. The primary member’s colleague retains an explicit overlap in the reference and single-member-withdrawal conditions. Shared records and duties to expose assumptions and disagreements apply across all conditions. Omission removes instructions, not a model’s latent knowledge; matching contribution slots does not match token volume or human effort.</p><p><a href="/agentic-le/roles/">Read the flower framework</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/experiments/">Explore the experiment studio</a></p></section>

    <section id="browser-evidence" aria-labelledby="browser-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Observed behavior · Separate from model ratings</p><h2 id="browser-title">What the browser checks actually covered</h2>
      <p>The fixed protocol checks initial rendering at three viewport sizes and exercises the same five desktop flows where the candidate provides the relevant controls. Each record is bound to the exact Build source, completed journal head, frozen harness, and executed interaction protocol.</p>
      <div class="coverage-grid"><div><strong>{qa.complete_initial_check_viewports}</strong><span>complete initial viewport observations</span></div><div><strong>{qa.observed_flow_count}</strong><span>observed F1–F5 flows</span></div><div><strong>{qa.runtime_errors_retained}</strong><span>retained runtime errors</span></div><div><strong>{qa.initial_overflow_viewports}</strong><span>initial viewports with horizontal overflow</span></div></div>
      <p class="small">Automated accessibility: {qa.automated_axe_violation_rule_occurrences} violation-rule occurrences and {qa.automated_axe_incomplete_rule_occurrences} incomplete-rule occurrences. {qa.automated_axe_unknown_viewports} viewports have unknown automated results. {qa.runtime_errors_dropped} runtime events were dropped by capture limits. {qa.initial_overflow_unknown_viewports} viewports have unknown overflow status.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Executed functional checks"><table><caption>Coverage states describe execution, not pedagogical success</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Common check</th><th scope="col">Recorded states</th></tr></thead><tbody>{CHECKS.map(([key,name]) => <tr><th scope="row">{key} · {name}</th><td>{Object.entries(qa.common_check_states?.[key] ?? {}).map(([status,count]) => `${status}: ${count}`).join(" · ") || "No bound observations"}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p><strong>“Observed” means the protocol executed and retained evidence.</strong> It is not a correctness score. A literal feedback change does not establish useful feedback; unchanged wording is interpreted with the actual inputs and the resource’s stated purpose. Missing controls, failed actions, and unexecuted steps remain explicit in each candidate’s coverage.</p>
      <p>The checks do not establish human learning, transfer, five-minute feasibility, a complete assistive-technology audit, or browser-wide deletion. Generic and functional reports are retained separately; their repeated initial checks are not counted as extra candidates.</p>
      <p><a href={`${base}publication-index.json`}>Inspect the public evidence index and source hashes</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="prototypes" aria-labelledby="prototypes-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">All planned candidates · Grouped by repetition</p><h2 id="prototypes-title">Inspect the retained solutions</h2></div><a href="#results">Back to results</a></div>
      <p>Every available preview uses the original retained Build source in an isolated frame with external resources and API requests blocked. Later generated plans are part of the review packet; proposed repairs do not alter these prototypes.</p>
      {view.repetitions.map(replicate => <details class="repetition" open={replicate === view.repetitions[0]}><summary>Repetition {replicate} · {index.candidates.filter(candidate => candidate.replicate === replicate).length} planned candidates</summary><div class="candidate-grid">{view.conditions.flatMap(condition => condition.candidates.filter(candidate => candidate.replicate === replicate)).map(candidate => {
        const review = view.reviews.get(candidate.item_id);
        const exclusion = view.excluded.get(candidate.item_id);
        return <article class="candidate-card" id={candidate.item_id}>
          <p class="eyebrow">Repetition {candidate.replicate} · {review ? "Included in review" : "Excluded from review"}</p><h3>{label(candidate.condition)}</h3>
          <p class="small">Original batch reports: {state(candidate.status)}.</p>
          <p class="candidate-title">{candidate.build?.title ?? "No evaluated Build preview"}</p>
          {review ? <dl class="candidate-indices">{AXES.map(([axis,name]) => <div><dt>{name}</dt><dd><strong>{number(review.axes[axis].mean_index)}</strong><span>Reviewer 1: {number(review.axes[axis].reviewer_indices[0])} · Reviewer 2: {number(review.axes[axis].reviewer_indices[1])}</span></dd></div>)}</dl> : <p class="missing-note">Review unavailable: {exclusion?.reason ?? "No review is included in the frozen set."}</p>}
          {candidate.build && <button class="open-candidate" data-source={`${base}${candidate.build.file}`} data-sha={candidate.build.sha256}>Open this candidate</button>}
          <p class="preview-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="preview-host"></div>
          <details class="candidate-detail"><summary>Browser coverage and evidence identity</summary><p>Functional record: {candidate.browser?.status ?? "Not available"}.</p><p>Generic record: {candidate.browser?.generic_status ?? "Not available"}{candidate.browser?.generic_qa_root === "study/qa/derived-results" ? " · supplemental evaluation-view checks" : candidate.browser?.generic_qa_root === "study/qa/results" ? " · original watcher checks" : ""}.</p><ul class="check-list">{CHECKS.map(([key,name]) => <li><span>{key} · {name}</span><strong>{checkState(candidate,key)}</strong></li>)}</ul>{candidate.browser?.issues?.length > 0 && <ul>{candidate.browser.issues.map(issue => <li>{issue}</li>)}</ul>}{candidate.build && <><p>Evaluation record: {recordLabel(candidate.build.journal_view.record_origin)}.</p><p>Exact HTML SHA-256</p><code>{candidate.build.sha256}</code><p>Build content hash</p><code>{candidate.build.content_hash}</code>{candidate.build.journal_view.provenance_sha256 && <><p>Evaluation-provenance file SHA-256</p><code>{candidate.build.journal_view.provenance_sha256}</code></>}</>}{review && <><p>Frozen evidence packet</p><code>{review.packet_hash}</code><p>Review states: {review.review_statuses.join("; ")}</p></>}</details>
        </article>;
      })}</div></details>)}
    </section>

    <section class="context-grid" aria-label="Interpretation and provenance">
      <article><h2>Limits on interpretation</h2><p>The evidence concerns one fictional scenario, the configured model and instructions, and a small set of generated candidates. Descriptive differences can inform further investigation; they do not establish causal effects in human teams or a population-level advantage.</p><p>The flower’s eight domains organize starting responsibilities around shared understanding. They are not an exhaustive taxonomy or a validated measurement of anyone’s expertise. Human flourishing support, system performance, and learning remain distinct views of the available design evidence.</p><p><a href="/agentic-le/paper/">Read methods, findings, and qualifications in the paper</a></p></article>
      <article><h2>Provenance and open evidence gaps</h2><ul>{index.audit.notes.map(note => <li>{note}</li>)}</ul><p>Primary journal hashes, instruction fidelity, receipt coverage, and raw-log consistency are separate checks. A verified source fingerprint does not resolve missing provider receipts or a disagreement between record copies.</p><p>Evaluation views derived from a strictly verified complete event-log extension: <strong>{index.record_origin_counts.complete_jsonl_extension ?? 0}</strong>. These separately labeled views preserve the incomplete primary snapshot’s metadata and the full recorded event chain, match the batch head, and introduce no event or response. Original files and generated HTML remain unchanged.</p><p><a href={`${base}audit-notes.json`}>Read the final audit counts and retained gaps</a></p><details><summary>Frozen identities</summary><p>Aggregate summary</p><code>{results.summary_hash}</code><p>Review freeze</p><code>{results.freeze_hash}</code><p>Generation audit source</p><code>{index.audit.source_sha256}</code><p>Functional protocol</p><code>{index.browser_summary.common_protocol_sha256}</code>{index.evaluation_manifest_hash && <><p>Evaluation-view manifest</p><code>{index.evaluation_manifest_hash}</code></>}</details></article>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<script is:inline type="module">
  import {createCandidatePreview} from '/agentic-le/experiments/artifact-view.js';
  async function openCandidate(button) {
    const card = button.closest('.candidate-card'), status = card.querySelector('.preview-status');
    if (button.disabled) return;
    button.disabled = true; status.textContent = 'Loading the retained source…';
    try {
      if (!button.dataset.source.endsWith('.txt')) throw new Error('The source must be served as plain text.');
      const response = await fetch(`${button.dataset.source}?v=${button.dataset.sha.slice(0, 12)}`);
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Source request returned ${response.status}.`);
      const bytes = await response.arrayBuffer(), digest = await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', bytes);
      const hash = [...new Uint8Array(digest)].map(value => value.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');
      if (hash !== button.dataset.sha) throw new Error('The source hash differs from the frozen evidence index.');
      const preview = createCandidatePreview(new TextDecoder('utf-8', {fatal: true}).decode(bytes));
      card.querySelector('.preview-host').replaceChildren(preview); card.classList.add('is-open');
      preview.querySelector('button').click(); button.hidden = true;
      status.textContent = 'Exact source verified. Isolated preview open; see the recorded scope of browser checks above.';
      card.scrollIntoView({behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start'});
    } catch (error) { status.textContent = `Preview could not open: ${error.message}`; button.disabled = false; }
  }
  document.querySelectorAll('.open-candidate').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => openCandidate(button)));
  document.querySelector('#copy-link').addEventListener('click', async () => {
    const status = document.querySelector('#copy-status'), link = `${location.origin}/agentic-le/flower-study/`;
    try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(link); status.textContent = 'Study link copied.'; }
    catch (error) { status.textContent = `Copy this link: ${link}`; }
  });
</script>

<style>
  .study-shell{max-width:76rem;margin:auto;padding:2rem var(--page-pad) 4rem}h1{max-width:58rem;font-size:clamp(2rem,4.4vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.12;margin:.4rem 0 1rem}h2{font-size:1.65rem}header>p{max-width:61rem}.study-banner{background:var(--tint-warm);border-left:4px solid var(--accent);border-radius:6px;padding:1.1rem 1.3rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.study-banner p{margin:.4rem 0 0;font-size:.95rem;max-width:none}.page-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.8rem 1.1rem;margin:1.5rem 0 2rem}button,.primary{font:600 .95rem var(--sans);padding:.65rem 1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:5px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer}.primary,.open-candidate{background:var(--ink);color:white;border-color:var(--ink);text-decoration:none}button:disabled{opacity:.65;cursor:wait}section{margin-top:2.8rem;scroll-margin-top:6rem}.metrics,.coverage-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1.4rem 0}.metrics>div,.coverage-grid>div{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem;background:var(--tint)}.metrics strong,.coverage-grid strong{display:block;font:700 clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem) var(--sans)}.metrics span,.coverage-grid span{display:block;font-size:.9rem;margin-top:.3rem}.table-scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:42rem}caption{text-align:left;font:600 .9rem var(--sans);padding:.75rem 0}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:.85rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}thead{background:var(--tint)}tbody th{font-weight:600;max-width:15rem}.cell-note{display:block;font-weight:400;font-size:.8rem;margin-top:.3rem}.index-value{font:700 1.2rem var(--sans)}.small,.method-detail{font-size:.9rem}.method-detail{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;margin:1.3rem 0}.method-detail p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600}.condition-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.condition-list article{border-top:3px solid var(--accent-2);padding:.8rem 0;scroll-margin-top:6rem}.condition-list h3{font-size:1.1rem;margin:.3rem 0}.condition-list p{font-size:.9rem}.section-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:1rem}.section-heading h2{margin:.25rem 0}.repetition{margin:1.2rem 0;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem}.repetition>summary{font-size:1.15rem}.candidate-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin-top:1.2rem}.candidate-card,.context-grid>article{min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1.3rem;background:var(--bg)}.candidate-card{scroll-margin-top:6rem}.candidate-card h3{font-size:1.35rem;margin:.4rem 0}.candidate-card.is-open{grid-column:1/-1}.candidate-title,.preview-status{font-size:.9rem}.candidate-indices{font-size:.88rem}.candidate-indices>div{padding:.6rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.candidate-indices dt{font-weight:600}.candidate-indices dd{margin:.2rem 0 0}.candidate-indices dd strong{font-size:1.1rem}.candidate-indices dd span{display:block;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted)}.candidate-detail{margin-top:1rem;font-size:.82rem}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:.75rem}.candidate-detail p{margin:.6rem 0 .3rem}.check-list{list-style:none;padding:0}.check-list li{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;padding:.3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.context-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem}.context-grid h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-top:0}.context-grid p,.context-grid li{font-size:.95rem}.context-grid li+li{margin-top:.6rem}.study-shell :global(.candidate-preview iframe){display:block;width:100%;height:760px;background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;margin:1rem 0}.study-shell :global(.candidate-preview pre){max-height:24rem;overflow:auto;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:.8rem}.study-shell :global(.candidate-preview .muted){font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)}figure{margin:2rem 0}figure img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}figcaption{font-size:.9rem;margin-top:.7rem}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible,.table-scroll:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent-2);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.metrics,.coverage-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.candidate-grid,.context-grid,.condition-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}.section-heading{align-items:start;flex-direction:column}.study-shell :global(.candidate-preview iframe){height:740px}.table-scroll{font-size:.9rem}.repetition{padding:.8rem}.candidate-card{padding:1rem}}@media print{.page-actions,.open-candidate,.preview-host{display:none}}
</style>
